<title>UK: Argentina sets 750 bln lire step-down 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Argentina sets 750 bln lire step-down 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Chase Manhatten.</p>
<p> BORROWER   REPUBLIC OF ARGENTINA</p>
<p> AMT    750 BLN LIRE  COUPON    *10.0	MATURITY    11.AUG.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.90    PAY DATE    11.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0	 REOFFER    99.50     SPREAD	+156 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *UNTIL AUG.1999 WHEN COUPON STEPS DOWN TO 7.625 PCT</p>
<p> MOODY	B1	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BB	  DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMS US/UK/IT/AR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.75	SELL CONC  1.25</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND OVER ITALIAN SWAP RATE.</p>
<p> NOTES	THERE IS AN OPTION FOR THE ISSUER TO REDENOMINATE</p>
<p>		INTO THE EURO IN THE THIRD STAGE OF EMU.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
